{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>They shall not be removed from it.</b> A verse contradicts: it is written ״the poles shall be in the rings of the ark״, and it is written ״and you shall bring the poles into the rings״ — thus they go in and out of them. How so? They slide back and forth but are not pulled out. Their ends were thick; they inserted one end with difficulty into the rings, but in the middle they were thin, so they were not tight in the rings but would slide back and forth, yet they would not slip out of them because their ends were thick. So it is taught, and so Rashi explained in chapter Ba Lo. Another interpretation: here and in the portion of ותכל it implies that Moses placed the poles in the ark, while in the portion of במדבר it is written ״and Aaron and his sons shall come and put its poles on״ — implying they were removed. One may answer that even though Moses placed them, HaShem desired that they be put on by the priests, as it is written ״and they shall put its poles on״, and from that time onward they shall not be removed from it. Because of its holiness, HaShem did not want them to grope at it to remove the poles and insert them into the rings. According to the plain sense, the poles fit tightly in the rings, so that when they carry the ark and go up mountains and down valleys, the ark will not slide down onto the shoulders of those who carry it. Or perhaps there are two grooves in each pole, and the rings are set in them. Another interpretation: <b>they shall not be removed from it</b> — according to the plain sense there is no need to remove these poles, for they cause no obstruction or crowding, since they are in the Holy of Holies, into which none enters and exits except the High Priest four times on one day in the year. But with the copper altar that stands in the courtyard, where everyone enters and exits — if the rings were there permanently, they would obstruct and crowd those entering and exiting; therefore the poles need only be there at the time of the journeys, as it is written ״and the poles shall be in the rings, etc.״ when carrying it."], :book :exodus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:00:27.486637150Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}